        "evidence": "No superlative wording, but one claim is vacuous as stated and worth reporting: \"it holds throughout the Wenzl positivity regime q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2} > 2 (which includes the substrate value q_0 approx 1.11)\". For any real q > 0, AM-GM gives q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2} >= 2 with equality only at q = 1, so this \"regime\" is every positive q except 1 - it excludes nothing. At q_0 = 1.1099785827513808 the value is 2.0027223639 (mpmath, 30 dps), i.e. it clears the bound by 0.0027, and the muon pin gives 2.0027223645, so the inequality also cannot discriminate the two q0 pins.",
